- **Persistence Update**: Modify `src/storage/json.ts` to handle an array of tasks in `tasks.json` (e.g., load/save as `Task[]`). Implement functions like `loadAllTasks()` for bulk retrieval and `saveTasks(tasks: Task[])` for atomic array persistence.
- **CLI Integration**: Add a `list` subcommand to `src/index.ts` using `commander`, with options: `--status <string>`, `--priority <string>`, `--tags <comma-separated>`, and `--search <query>` for free-text matching on objective/metadata. Implement filtering logic in a new `src/commands/list.ts` module, outputting results as formatted JSON or table via `console.log`. Add a `view` subcommand for detailed single-task viewing by ID (e.g., `taskforge view --id <number>`).
- **Filtering Logic**: Use array methods (e.g., `filter()`) for status/priority exact matches, tag intersection checks, and case-insensitive regex for free-text search. Ensure queries are composable (e.g., combine multiple filters).

Code snippet for list command and filtering:
```typescript
// src/commands/list.ts
import { Task } from '../models/task';
import { loadAllTasks } from '../storage/json';

export async function listTasks(filters: { status?: string; priority?: string; tags?: string[]; search?: string }): Promise<Task[]> {
  const tasks = await loadAllTasks();
  return tasks.filter(task => {
    if (filters.status && task.status !== filters.status) return false;
    if (filters.priority && task.priority !== filters.priority) return false;
    if (filters.tags && !filters.tags.every(tag => task.tags.includes(tag))) return false;
    if (filters.search) {
      const regex = new RegExp(filters.search, 'i');
      if (!regex.test(task.objective) && !regex.test(JSON.stringify(task.metadata))) return false;
    }
    return true;
  });
}

// In src/index.ts (commander setup)
program
  .command('list')
  .option('--status <string>')
  .option('--priority <string>')
  .option('--tags <string>')
  .option('--search <string>')
  .action(async (options) => {
    const filters = { ...options, tags: options.tags?.split(',') };
    const results = await listTasks(filters);
    console.log(JSON.stringify(results, null, 2));
  });
```

